  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "Spring leaves are mid chocolate-brown with light green veining and covered with a soft pubescence. They become an unusual dark olive-green by early summer and then turn bronze-green. Fall color is orange-yellow. The current shoots are covered in a gray bloom. The large leaves have seven to nine deeply incised ovate lobes with tail-like pointed tips. The margins have conspicuous, sharply pointed, hooked teeth. This strong-growing upright cultivar reaches up to 26 ft. (8 m) tall and wide. It was named after a granddaughter of Dutch nurseryman D. M. van Gelderen."
  },
